  "articleBody": "Embarking on a kitchen addition can be exciting, but it's easy to stumble into common traps that can cause delays and headaches. One big one is underestimating the time it takes to get all your approvals. Permit review can add weeks or even months, so don't start any demolition until you have everything signed off. Another frequent mistake is ordering materials too late. Lead times can vary wildly, and you don't want your project stalled waiting for that perfect countertop. And speaking of delays, failing to account for your builder's availability can really push back your start date. Good contractors are often booked up, so lock in your team early! It’s super important to choose a builder who can handle the whole shebang: drawings, approvals, structural work, and coordinating all the different trades. Make sure they provide a written contract and a realistic schedule too. At HH Remodeling LLC, serving the Denver area, we pride ourselves on clear communication and helping you avoid these common pitfalls, ensuring your kitchen addition goes as smoothly as possible.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}